/ The anchor makes the files section linkable (#attachments). Redmine gives
/ #relations and #issue_tree one, the attachments block never had one - and
/ since this override owns the block, this is the only place it can live.
/ Collapsed and expanded case share it, so a link works either way.
- if @issue.attachments.any?
  #attachments
    - max_files = Additionals.setting :issue_hide_max_attachments
    - file_count = @issue.attachments.length
    - if max_files.present? && file_count > max_files.to_i
      fieldset.collapsible.collapsed.hide-attachments
        legend.icon.icon-collapsed onclick='toggleFieldset(this);'
          = sprite_icon 'angle-right', rtl: true
          strong = label_with_count :label_attachment_plural, file_count
        .hidden
          = link_to_attachments @issue, thumbnails: true
      / Jumping straight at the anchor has to show the files, not just their
      / heading - otherwise the link lands on a closed drawer.
      javascript:
        $(function() {
          if (window.location.hash === '#attachments') {
            $('#attachments fieldset.hide-attachments.collapsed legend').each(function() { toggleFieldset(this); });
          }
        });
    - else
      hr
      p
        strong = l :label_attachment_plural
      = link_to_attachments @issue, thumbnails: true
